# Optional: annadata-app (internal client)

This plugin is **published and installed independently** (`npm install llama-cpp-capacitor`). The sibling app below is only used for Annadata's own product QA — not required for other developers.

```
Project_A/
  annadata-llama-cpp/   ← plugin (you are here)
  annadata-app/         ← optional internal Ionic client
```

## Standard install (any Capacitor app)

```bash
npm install llama-cpp-capacitor
npx cap sync ios    # or android
```

**iOS simulator:** from your app root (macOS + Xcode + cmake):

```bash
bash node_modules/llama-cpp-capacitor/scripts/ensure-llama-ios-xcframework.sh
npx cap sync ios
```

**Release / pack:** `npm run build:package && npm run verify:pack:artifacts`

## Internal-only sync (Annadata dev)

When `../annadata-app` exists, run sync from **the app repo** (not here):

```bash
cd ../annadata-app
npm run sync:llama-cpp:wasm     # WASM → public/llama-wasm (after build:pwa:full here)
npm run sync:llama-cpp:native   # pack + reinstall + cap sync
```

Native runtime loads via `LlamaNativeBridge` (`dlopen` on `llama-cpp.framework/llama-cpp`). `Package.swift` is Swift-only — no SPM binaryTarget path dependency.
